1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:06,538
Six days after graduating dead last, Naruto Uzumaki is doing the Hokage's paperwork.

2
00:00:06,538 --> 00:00:10,009
All of it. With two hundred copies of himself.

3
00:00:10,227 --> 00:00:14,026
[CLONE] Boss, this report just stops in the middle of a sentence. Is that normal?

4
00:00:14,170 --> 00:00:15,779
[NARUTO] Yeah. Read the next one.

5
00:00:16,017 --> 00:00:20,105
Twenty years of mission reports. Every ambush. Every mistake.

6
00:00:20,105 --> 00:00:24,261
Every ninja who never came home. And he'll remember all of it.

7
00:00:24,485 --> 00:00:28,853
Because every shadow clone sends its memories back when it pops.

8
00:00:28,853 --> 00:00:33,699
That's not a what-if. In canon, nobody tells Naruto until he's sixteen.

9
00:00:33,941 --> 00:00:37,588
So this isn't a power-up story. The rule is simple.

10
00:00:37,588 --> 00:00:41,020
He does not get stronger. He gets to read first.

11
00:00:41,271 --> 00:00:47,963
That's six days from now. Tonight he's twelve, filthy, and alone in a forest with a stolen scroll.

12
00:00:47,963 --> 00:00:50,490
And he's about to read one more line.

13
00:00:53,473 --> 00:00:56,627
Midnight. A clearing deep in the forest.

14
00:00:56,627 --> 00:01:01,437
Naruto has a hundred bruises and, at last, one perfect clone.

15
00:01:01,669 --> 00:01:05,908
[NARUTO] Okay. Okay! Look at that. It even has my stupid face.

16
00:01:06,051 --> 00:01:08,655
[CLONE] That's my stupid face! Boss, we did it!

17
00:01:08,797 --> 00:01:10,201
They grin at each other.

18
00:01:10,201 --> 00:01:14,706
The clone steps back to celebrate, and the root behind him doesn't step back.

19
00:01:14,965 --> 00:01:16,444
[CLONE] Whoa, whoa, whoa—

20
00:01:16,575 --> 00:01:22,419
Pop. Ten feet away, Naruto yelps and grabs his own knee. It's scraped raw.

21
00:01:22,655 --> 00:01:25,164
[NARUTO] Ow. Wait. I didn't fall.

22
00:01:25,690 --> 00:01:26,605
He looks down.

23
00:01:26,605 --> 00:01:32,554
Under the hand seals, in cramped brushwork, there's a note he was about to roll right past.

24
00:01:32,797 --> 00:01:40,061
The Shadow Clone Jutsu was invented by the Second Hokage, Tobirama, for scouting enemy ground.

25
00:01:40,061 --> 00:01:42,611
Naruto learned it in a few hours.

26
00:01:42,857 --> 00:01:47,564
The note is six lines long. What the clone learns, the caster keeps.

27
00:01:47,564 --> 00:01:53,586
For this reason the technique is forbidden. The mind fails long before the chakra does.

28
00:01:54,185 --> 00:01:57,764
[NARUTO] So everything he learns, I learn. Everything.

29
00:01:58,010 --> 00:02:03,497
A twelve year old with more chakra than anyone alive has just found a cheat code.

30
00:02:03,497 --> 00:02:04,649
Four years early.

31
00:02:04,875 --> 00:02:07,843
He doesn't celebrate. He runs an experiment.

32
00:02:07,843 --> 00:02:12,564
One clone, the next page of the scroll, and a long walk around a tree.

33
00:02:12,783 --> 00:02:14,987
[CLONE] Pop me when I'm done. I wanna see if it works!

34
00:02:14,917 --> 00:02:20,671
[CLONE] Reading, reading. Ooh, this seal is nasty. Okay, I see how it works.

35
00:02:20,786 --> 00:02:26,910
Naruto pokes him with a stick. Pop. And he knows the seal. Not read it. Knows it.

36
00:02:27,113 --> 00:02:29,517
[NARUTO] Wait. I can be in two classes at once.

37
00:02:29,772 --> 00:02:31,881
[NARUTO] Ya know what? I can be in all of them!

38
00:02:32,112 --> 00:02:35,771
[IRUKA] Naruto! There you are! Do you have any idea what you've done?

39
00:02:35,981 --> 00:02:40,490
[NARUTO] Mizuki-sensei? You said if I learned one jutsu from this, I'd pass!

40
00:02:40,634 --> 00:02:44,752
[MIZUKI] Give me the scroll, Naruto. You've done exactly what I needed.

41
00:02:44,752 --> 00:02:47,343
[MIZUKI] It was never meant for a fool like you.

42
00:02:47,567 --> 00:02:51,568
[MIZUKI] Twelve years ago the Nine Tails destroyed this village.

43
00:02:51,568 --> 00:02:55,206
[MIZUKI] And you're the fox, Naruto. Everyone knew but you.

44
00:02:55,426 --> 00:03:00,136
Mizuki hurls a giant shuriken at the boy. Naruto can't move.

45
00:03:00,136 --> 00:03:05,475
It never lands. Iruka is over him, the blade buried in his own back.

46
00:03:05,691 --> 00:03:07,552
Naruto goes very still.

47
00:03:07,552 --> 00:03:13,055
Iruka, bleeding, doesn't look at the boy at all. He looks at Mizuki.

48
00:03:13,298 --> 00:03:19,102
[IRUKA] He's not the demon fox. He's Naruto Uzumaki of the Hidden Leaf. And he's my student.

49
00:03:19,615 --> 00:03:24,681
Mizuki charges. Naruto answers with the one jutsu he learned tonight.

50
00:03:24,681 --> 00:03:27,764
The clearing fills with a thousand of him.

51
00:03:27,964 --> 00:03:31,023
[CLONE] Come on, Mizuki! Pick one! Pick any one!

52
00:03:31,180 --> 00:03:34,183
Mizuki goes down under a mountain of orange.

53
00:03:34,183 --> 00:03:38,824
Then the clones disperse, and a thousand memories come home at once.

54
00:03:39,046 --> 00:03:43,721
The same moment, from a thousand angles. Mizuki's fist.

55
00:03:43,721 --> 00:03:48,650
The moon. And Iruka's face, crying, a thousand times over.

56
00:03:49,239 --> 00:03:54,548
The first person who ever chose him. And Naruto gets to keep every single copy.

57
00:03:54,769 --> 00:04:00,438
He drops to his knees and is sick in the grass. Iruka thinks it's chakra exhaustion.

58
00:04:00,651 --> 00:04:03,610
[IRUKA] Easy. Breathe. You overdid it, that's all.

59
00:04:03,740 --> 00:04:07,629
[NARUTO] It's not that, sensei. I just saw your face. A thousand times.

60
00:04:07,835 --> 00:04:10,644
[IRUKA] Close your eyes, Naruto. I've something for you.

61
00:04:10,889 --> 00:04:12,848
[IRUKA] Congratulations. You graduate.

62
00:04:13,048 --> 00:04:15,622
[NARUTO] That's your headband. You can't give me your headband!

63
00:04:15,752 --> 00:04:18,376
[IRUKA] I can get another one. You only graduate once.

64
00:04:18,586 --> 00:04:20,680
[NARUTO] Nobody ever stayed to see me finish anything.

65
00:04:20,933 --> 00:04:22,252
[IRUKA] Then I'll stay for the next one.

66
00:04:22,469 --> 00:04:25,732
Everyone else remembers one graduation night.

67
00:04:25,732 --> 00:04:28,923
Naruto gets to remember it a thousand times.

68
00:04:31,839 --> 00:04:33,709
Morning. He should be asleep.

69
00:04:33,709 --> 00:04:38,288
Instead he's on the Academy roof with twenty clones, testing the rules.

70
00:04:38,513 --> 00:04:45,037
Rule one. The knowing comes back. The muscles don't. Skill yes, strength no.

71
00:04:45,276 --> 00:04:49,935
[CLONE] Okay, rule three. A clone that gets hit pops. So who's gonna get punched?

72
00:04:49,865 --> 00:04:51,824
[CLONE] Not me. I got punched last time.

73
00:04:51,754 --> 00:04:52,743
[CLONE] You're the same person!

74
00:04:52,673 --> 00:04:54,032
[CLONE] Then it doesn't matter who!

75
00:04:54,174 --> 00:05:00,576
Somebody gets punched. Pop. On the roof, Naruto winces for a face that isn't his.

76
00:05:00,576 --> 00:05:03,738
Rule three, confirmed. He keeps the hit.

77
00:05:03,944 --> 00:05:07,378
[NARUTO] Okay. We all feel it. Nobody gets punched twice!

78
00:05:07,538 --> 00:05:11,597
[CLONE] Rule four. Every clone carries a share of my chakra.

79
00:05:11,527 --> 00:05:12,606
[CLONE] Then why do I feel hungry?

80
00:05:12,741 --> 00:05:15,160
[NARUTO] Because we're all hungry. We're one stomach.

81
00:05:15,283 --> 00:05:17,461
Rule four he underlines twice.

82
00:05:17,461 --> 00:05:22,617
Every clone carries a share of his chakra. And his chakra has a lodger.

83
00:05:22,818 --> 00:05:28,349
Rule two is less funny. Every clone's tiredness comes back too, all at once.

84
00:05:28,349 --> 00:05:31,987
Fifty clones for an hour is a fifty hour headache.

85
00:05:32,220 --> 00:05:35,899
[CLONE] Boss. One hour. Everyone pops at the same time, right?

86
00:05:36,029 --> 00:05:37,098
[NARUTO] That's the plan.

87
00:05:37,240 --> 00:05:38,414
[CLONE] That's a terrible plan.

88
00:05:38,524 --> 00:05:40,103
[NARUTO] Everybody dispel on three!

89
00:05:40,246 --> 00:05:43,050
[CLONE] Wait. Is it on three, or after three?

90
00:05:43,167 --> 00:05:45,471
[NARUTO] It's on three! Why is that hard?!

91
00:05:45,618 --> 00:05:50,748
He tries it anyway. Fifty clones, one hour, all dispelled together.

92
00:05:50,748 --> 00:05:53,887
Naruto is unconscious for nineteen hours.

93
00:05:54,476 --> 00:05:57,050
[NARUTO] Ugh. Why is there a crow on my chest?

94
00:05:57,191 --> 00:05:59,895
[NARUTO] Okay. Batches. Batches of ten.

95
00:06:00,147 --> 00:06:04,081
[NARUTO] Right. Every class I ever slept through. Everything I missed. Go!

96
00:06:04,285 --> 00:06:07,787
Twenty clones take notes in the back of every classroom.

97
00:06:07,787 --> 00:06:12,164
Somewhere a teacher wonders why his worst student has so many cousins.

98
00:06:12,380 --> 00:06:15,261
The library throws him out. He's that boy.

99
00:06:15,261 --> 00:06:20,269
So thirty clones walk back in, transformed into thirty different old men.

100
00:06:20,500 --> 00:06:24,129
[CLONE] Good afternoon, sir. Where might I find the chakra control primer?

101
00:06:24,059 --> 00:06:26,418
[CLONE] What a coincidence. I'm also looking for that book.

102
00:06:26,566 --> 00:06:31,540
One librarian notices that all thirty old men are reading the same beginner's primer.

103
00:06:31,540 --> 00:06:33,880
Four of them are holding it upside down.

104
00:06:34,431 --> 00:06:37,282
Then leaf exercises, times two hundred.

105
00:06:37,282 --> 00:06:41,375
And he finally learns why his clone jutsu always failed.

106
00:06:41,590 --> 00:06:45,954
[NARUTO] It was never too little chakra! It was way too much, shoved through a pinhole!

107
00:06:46,166 --> 00:06:51,795
Two hundred clones, ten hours each. That's two thousand hours of practice a day.

108
00:06:51,795 --> 00:06:54,820
Most genin don't train that much in a year.

109
00:06:55,078 --> 00:07:00,161
That evening Iruka takes him to Ichiraku, the way he does when he's worried.

110
00:07:00,161 --> 00:07:04,642
Naruto orders his usual and, for once, chews with his mouth closed.

111
00:07:04,895 --> 00:07:07,324
[IRUKA] Eat slower. Nobody's going to take your bowl.

112
00:07:07,441 --> 00:07:08,270
[NARUTO] Old habit.

113
00:07:08,414 --> 00:07:11,518
[IRUKA] Quick question, Naruto. Who founded the Hidden Leaf?

114
00:07:11,653 --> 00:07:14,508
[NARUTO] Hashirama Senju and Madara Uchiha.

115
00:07:14,508 --> 00:07:20,217
[NARUTO] Then the Second Hokage, Tobirama. Who invented my jutsu, by the way.

116
00:07:20,457 --> 00:07:22,476
[IRUKA] Say that again. Slowly.

117
00:07:22,605 --> 00:07:25,054
[IRUKA] Naruto. Where did you learn all this?

118
00:07:25,284 --> 00:07:29,403
[NARUTO] Everywhere. Mostly the library. They're really nice there, once you're old.

119
00:07:29,516 --> 00:07:32,673
He knows which shops will serve him, and at what hour.

120
00:07:32,673 --> 00:07:37,000
He knows people by their footsteps, because nobody ever walked toward him.

121
00:07:37,249 --> 00:07:38,578
On the tower above,

122
00:07:38,578 --> 00:07:43,193
the Third Hokage watches it all in his crystal ball, pipe in hand.

123
00:07:43,412 --> 00:07:46,414
His left hand has formed a cross seal on the desk.

124
00:07:46,414 --> 00:07:49,116
He doesn't seem to notice. It's an old habit.

125
00:07:49,375 --> 00:07:54,994
[HIRUZEN] Two thousand hours a day. Hm. That explains the librarian.

126
00:07:55,210 --> 00:07:57,986
He isn't angry. He's doing the same arithmetic.

127
00:07:57,986 --> 00:08:00,644
And looking at the paperwork on his own desk.

128
00:08:03,530 --> 00:08:05,287
The summons comes at dawn.

129
00:08:05,287 --> 00:08:09,409
Naruto walks into the Hokage's office braced to be yelled at.

130
00:08:09,657 --> 00:08:12,242
[NARUTO] Old man, I can explain! Okay, I can't.

131
00:08:12,242 --> 00:08:16,051
[NARUTO] But I learned a jutsu, so technically I passed, ya know!

132
00:08:16,207 --> 00:08:20,643
[HIRUZEN] Stealing the Scroll of Seals is a crime, Naruto.

133
00:08:20,643 --> 00:08:25,726
[HIRUZEN] The sentence is one month of filing duty in my archive.

134
00:08:25,982 --> 00:08:31,776
[HIRUZEN] Unclassified mission reports only. Every shelf, every box.

135
00:08:31,899 --> 00:08:33,898
[NARUTO] Filing?! I'm a ninja now!

136
00:08:34,035 --> 00:08:36,064
[HIRUZEN] Then file like one.

137
00:08:36,637 --> 00:08:39,431
[NARUTO] A month? Old man, I could do a month in a day.

138
00:08:39,563 --> 00:08:42,597
[HIRUZEN] I know. That's rather the point.

139
00:08:42,822 --> 00:08:44,241
[NARUTO] Can I at least have a lunch break?

140
00:08:44,383 --> 00:08:49,732
[HIRUZEN] You may have an hour. Your clones may have the next five.

141
00:08:49,970 --> 00:08:58,464
[HIRUZEN] First, a staff form. Name, office, position. Paperwork, Naruto. Get used to it.

142
00:08:58,665 --> 00:09:03,654
[NARUTO] Fine. Filing clerk. Naruto Uzumaki. Where's the punishment part?

143
00:09:03,798 --> 00:09:05,292
[HIRUZEN] You're standing in it.

144
00:09:05,412 --> 00:09:08,884
It's the first official form that has ever carried his name,

145
00:09:08,884 --> 00:09:10,851
and he signs it twice by accident.

146
00:09:11,057 --> 00:09:15,251
The Third's reasons are two. Keep the boy where the old man can see him.

147
00:09:15,456 --> 00:09:17,724
And let a lonely child be, for once,

148
00:09:17,724 --> 00:09:20,875
inside the building instead of outside the window.

149
00:09:21,405 --> 00:09:27,999
Day one. Two hundred Narutos enter the archive. It is, structurally, a fire hazard.

150
00:09:28,235 --> 00:09:31,694
[CLONE] Pass it down! Pass it down! Do not drop it, it's older than us!

151
00:09:31,624 --> 00:09:33,143
[CLONE] Why is there a stamp on your forehead?

152
00:09:33,073 --> 00:09:34,427
[CLONE] He needed a flat surface!

153
00:09:34,357 --> 00:09:37,596
[CLONE] I found a portrait of somebody very old. Where does it go?

154
00:09:37,526 --> 00:09:38,685
[CLONE] With the other old things.

155
00:09:38,615 --> 00:09:40,299
[CLONE] That's the Third Hokage.

156
00:09:40,229 --> 00:09:41,608
[CLONE] Do not say that out loud!

157
00:09:41,538 --> 00:09:43,892
[CLONE] Boss, where do I put the Hokage's hat?

158
00:09:44,024 --> 00:09:45,023
[NARUTO] Under H!

159
00:09:45,169 --> 00:09:46,918
[CLONE] For Hat or for Hokage?

160
00:09:47,030 --> 00:09:48,249
[NARUTO] Yes! Both!

161
00:09:48,395 --> 00:09:56,174
By noon, a bucket chain of clones is passing scrolls from the basement to the third floor, out one window and in through another.

162
00:09:56,174 --> 00:09:58,284
Nobody tells them there are stairs.

163
00:09:58,524 --> 00:10:04,088
By night, the Third Hokage's in tray is empty. For the first time in thirty years.

164
00:10:04,343 --> 00:10:07,577
[NARUTO] Old man! Your in-tray's empty. What do we do now?

165
00:10:07,777 --> 00:10:11,306
[HIRUZEN] I don't know. That has never happened.

166
00:10:11,462 --> 00:10:15,161
[HIRUZEN] Is that my desk? I'd forgotten it was wood.

167
00:10:15,299 --> 00:10:21,190
Years from now, as Seventh Hokage, Naruto will run this same office with shadow clones.

168
00:10:21,190 --> 00:10:22,883
He's just starting early.

169
00:10:23,125 --> 00:10:24,354
Then the mail desk.

170
00:10:24,354 --> 00:10:29,464
Diplomatic letters from every hidden village, sorted by hand and filed by date.

171
00:10:29,680 --> 00:10:33,242
[CLONE] Boss, why does the Fourth Kazekage sign like he's stabbing the page?

172
00:10:33,352 --> 00:10:37,091
[NARUTO] He presses so hard the brush splits. Look at every downstroke!

173
00:10:37,235 --> 00:10:42,914
[HIRUZEN] Ha. He has always been a hard man. File it under S for Sand.

174
00:10:43,149 --> 00:10:46,673
[NARUTO] Old man, can I keep that letter? It's the best thing I've ever read.

175
00:10:46,786 --> 00:10:50,025
[HIRUZEN] No. It's a diplomatic document.

176
00:10:50,158 --> 00:10:51,017
[NARUTO] Worth a shot.

177
00:10:51,176 --> 00:10:55,142
Naruto thinks it's the funniest thing he has read all week.

178
00:10:55,142 --> 00:10:58,235
He files it under S, and moves on to the next.

179
00:10:58,493 --> 00:11:04,652
As punishments go, it is a strange one. Nobody has ever handed Naruto a key before.

180
00:11:07,538 --> 00:11:15,096
On the second day, the Third Hokage walks past the archive door and counts forty Narutos reading in complete silence.

181
00:11:15,096 --> 00:11:18,067
He keeps walking. Then he walks back to check.

182
00:11:18,283 --> 00:11:21,150
By the fourth day, it stops being funny.

183
00:11:21,150 --> 00:11:25,522
Mission reports aren't stories. They're after-action reports.

184
00:11:25,769 --> 00:11:29,011
Every ambush that worked. Every formation that failed.

185
00:11:29,011 --> 00:11:32,073
Every report that ends in the middle of a sentence.

186
00:11:32,320 --> 00:11:37,130
[CLONE] Boss. Three separate reports on one cat. The last one just says, never again.

187
00:11:37,241 --> 00:11:39,050
[NARUTO] File them under tragedies.

188
00:11:39,170 --> 00:11:42,279
[CLONE] Boss, here's one where the cat bit a chunin. Pretty hard.

189
00:11:42,393 --> 00:11:43,552
[NARUTO] Respect the cat.

190
00:11:43,666 --> 00:11:47,665
[NARUTO] Every ambush has the same shape. They always hit the last man first.

191
00:11:47,874 --> 00:11:49,468
[CLONE] So we put somebody useless at the back.

192
00:11:49,598 --> 00:11:52,802
[NARUTO] Nobody's useless at the back. Put somebody who's paying attention.

193
00:11:53,040 --> 00:11:57,069
[NARUTO] Look. Three teams were hit on the same road. Always the same corner.

194
00:11:57,283 --> 00:11:58,902
[CLONE] So somebody should have checked the corner.

195
00:11:59,021 --> 00:12:02,500
[NARUTO] Somebody did. They wrote it down. Nobody read it.

196
00:12:02,727 --> 00:12:05,001
[CLONE] Boss. Why does nobody read these?

197
00:12:05,160 --> 00:12:07,504
[NARUTO] 'Cause it's easier to be brave than to be prepared.

198
00:12:07,709 --> 00:12:10,598
[CLONE] Boss, two reports disagree about the same fight.

199
00:12:10,725 --> 00:12:14,064
[NARUTO] Then one of them was scared, or both were. Read both.

200
00:12:14,306 --> 00:12:17,340
[CLONE] Boss. This one is signed by somebody who never came back.

201
00:12:17,540 --> 00:12:20,094
[NARUTO] Read the names out loud. Somebody oughta.

202
00:12:20,302 --> 00:12:24,330
Two hundred voices read them aloud, quietly, one after another.

203
00:12:24,330 --> 00:12:26,696
Nobody has done that for any of them.

204
00:12:27,240 --> 00:12:29,925
Most genin learn from one teacher.

205
00:12:29,925 --> 00:12:36,164
Naruto is learning from every shinobi who ever came home. And a few who didn't.

206
00:12:36,395 --> 00:12:37,348
He goes quiet.

207
00:12:37,348 --> 00:12:43,064
For the first time in his life, Naruto Uzumaki isn't the loudest person in the room.

208
00:12:43,317 --> 00:12:49,066
[CLONE] Boss. C-rank escort. The last line says, puddle on the road, no rain for a week.

209
00:12:49,291 --> 00:12:50,972
[NARUTO] Mark that one. Don't ask me why.

210
00:12:50,972 --> 00:12:53,860
[NARUTO] It just feels like a sentence that's got a second half.

211
00:12:54,068 --> 00:12:56,207
He starts to read what isn't there.

212
00:12:56,207 --> 00:13:01,952
One week in October, twelve years ago, where every file is in a different clerk's handwriting.

213
00:13:02,155 --> 00:13:05,764
[CLONE] Boss, that whole shelf is marked off limits. By the Third himself.

214
00:13:06,017 --> 00:13:08,781
[NARUTO] Off limits. Huh. Leave it. For now.

215
00:13:09,026 --> 00:13:11,975
[IRUKA] Naruto, it's midnight. Go home.

216
00:13:12,209 --> 00:13:14,623
[NARUTO] One more shelf, sensei. Please.

217
00:13:14,775 --> 00:13:15,689
[IRUKA] Are all of those you?

218
00:13:15,810 --> 00:13:17,894
[NARUTO] Yes. Do not tell the old man.

219
00:13:18,007 --> 00:13:22,021
[IRUKA] Naruto. The old man signed your form. He knows.

220
00:13:22,253 --> 00:13:27,975
Then, on the sixth day, a clone in the back corner finds a thin folder.

221
00:13:27,975 --> 00:13:31,602
Kakashi Hatake. Jonin instructor evaluations.

222
00:13:31,820 --> 00:13:34,515
Kakashi Hatake has never passed a team.

223
00:13:34,515 --> 00:13:38,729
Every genin he ever tested went straight back to the Academy.

224
00:13:38,963 --> 00:13:43,142
[CLONE] Boss, every one says the same thing. Failed. Could not work together.

225
00:13:43,393 --> 00:13:46,997
[CLONE] And eleven reports say Kakashi Hatake arrived late. Eleven.

226
00:13:47,137 --> 00:13:49,046
[NARUTO] So he's late a lot. So what?

227
00:13:49,164 --> 00:13:50,638
[CLONE] No. Look at the dates.

228
00:13:50,771 --> 00:13:54,915
[NARUTO] Huh. Same dates. Every year. Nobody's that unlucky.

229
00:13:55,144 --> 00:13:58,126
He writes the dates in the margin of his notebook.

230
00:13:58,126 --> 00:14:01,823
Then, because tomorrow is team assignments, he turns the page.

231
00:14:02,056 --> 00:14:04,952
Most students walk into a test with a pencil.

232
00:14:04,952 --> 00:14:08,170
Naruto will walk in with the teacher's whole file.

233
00:14:11,024 --> 00:14:13,841
Team Seven. Naruto, Sasuke, Sakura.

234
00:14:13,841 --> 00:14:23,258
Their jonin instructor, Kakashi Hatake, orders them to the training ground at dawn for a survival test. No breakfast.

235
00:14:23,474 --> 00:14:28,343
Kakashi Hatake will not be there at dawn. He is late to everything.

236
00:14:28,584 --> 00:14:31,066
Naruto knows. It's in eleven reports.

237
00:14:31,066 --> 00:14:35,963
Which gives him the training ground, three hours, and two hundred clones.

238
00:14:36,206 --> 00:14:39,976
By the time the others arrive there are fourteen wires,

239
00:14:39,976 --> 00:14:43,060
six trenches, and one very confused squirrel.

240
00:14:43,296 --> 00:14:45,315
[CLONE] Boss, the squirrel is still in the net.

241
00:14:45,451 --> 00:14:46,995
[NARUTO] Leave him. He's a witness.

242
00:14:47,134 --> 00:14:48,938
[SASUKE] Why are you standing in a ditch?

243
00:14:49,090 --> 00:14:51,523
[NARUTO] Listen, both of you. It's a teamwork test.

244
00:14:51,523 --> 00:14:55,579
[NARUTO] He's failed every team before us. I know 'cause I filed the paperwork.

245
00:14:55,818 --> 00:14:58,387
[SASUKE] You're dead last. Why would I believe you?

246
00:14:58,622 --> 00:15:00,851
[SAKURA] Nobody knows what the test is, Naruto.

247
00:15:00,851 --> 00:15:03,961
[SAKURA] And honestly? You're annoying. Why would I trust you?

248
00:15:04,091 --> 00:15:07,855
[NARUTO] Because I've never lied to you. Okay, three times. This isn't one of them.

249
00:15:08,101 --> 00:15:09,755
[SAKURA] If this goes wrong, I'm blaming you.

250
00:15:09,893 --> 00:15:12,397
[NARUTO] Fair. Blame me. I'll be right next to you.

251
00:15:12,510 --> 00:15:13,789
[SASUKE] I don't need a team.

252
00:15:14,033 --> 00:15:16,752
[NARUTO] Good. Me neither. I just need you to listen.

253
00:15:16,974 --> 00:15:20,472
Knowing the answer is useless if nobody will listen.

254
00:15:20,472 --> 00:15:23,298
The obstacle was never power. It is trust.

255
00:15:23,784 --> 00:15:27,450
[NARUTO] Fine. Here's the deal. Whatever bells we get, you two take them.

256
00:15:27,450 --> 00:15:30,028
[NARUTO] I'll be the one who goes back to the Academy.

257
00:15:30,259 --> 00:15:31,798
[NARUTO] I just need two of us to pass.

258
00:15:32,031 --> 00:15:34,260
[SAKURA] Naruto. You would really do that?

259
00:15:34,510 --> 00:15:38,314
[SASUKE] Hm. Fine. Stop talking and show me the plan.

260
00:15:38,560 --> 00:15:44,327
Kakashi strolls in, book open, and finds three genin waiting in a perfect triangle.

261
00:15:44,327 --> 00:15:45,439
He turns a page.

262
00:15:45,696 --> 00:15:49,270
[KAKASHI] Sorry I'm late. I got lost on the road of life.

263
00:15:49,408 --> 00:15:55,522
[KAKASHI] Two bells. Three of you. Whoever has none goes back to the Academy. Begin.

264
00:15:55,746 --> 00:16:00,761
[KAKASHI] Come at me with the intent to kill. It's the only way you'll ever touch me.

265
00:16:00,965 --> 00:16:03,139
[SAKURA] Is he serious? He can't be serious.

266
00:16:03,261 --> 00:16:05,235
[SASUKE] He's serious. Get ready.

267
00:16:05,375 --> 00:16:06,381
Nobody moves.

268
00:16:06,381 --> 00:16:13,034
Then Sasuke opens with a fireball, and Kakashi, for the first time today, has to move.

269
00:16:13,272 --> 00:16:16,588
He lands on a wire Naruto strung at dawn.

270
00:16:16,588 --> 00:16:20,146
Sakura's kunai cuts it, and a log swings in.

271
00:16:20,390 --> 00:16:25,429
Kakashi dodges the log, then the kunai, then the second log nobody told him about.

272
00:16:25,429 --> 00:16:28,809
He's still holding the book. He's no longer reading it.

273
00:16:29,058 --> 00:16:31,685
[KAKASHI] Not bad. Whoever planned that.

274
00:16:31,842 --> 00:16:34,853
Then Sasuke throws a windmill shuriken.

275
00:16:34,853 --> 00:16:39,176
Kakashi sidesteps it, bored. And the shuriken is Naruto.

276
00:16:39,762 --> 00:16:46,546
In canon, Naruto pulls this exact trick on Zabuza, months from now. He's just early.

277
00:16:46,774 --> 00:16:51,633
A hand closes around a bell. Kakashi's one visible eye goes wide.

278
00:16:52,210 --> 00:16:54,449
[KAKASHI] Wait. Who taught you that?

279
00:16:54,650 --> 00:16:55,614
[NARUTO] A lot of me.

280
00:16:56,196 --> 00:16:57,830
[NARUTO] Sasuke. Catch.

281
00:16:57,972 --> 00:16:59,166
[SASUKE] You're giving it to me?

282
00:16:59,287 --> 00:17:02,066
[NARUTO] I said I would. Two of us have to pass.

283
00:17:02,314 --> 00:17:06,778
[KAKASHI] You'd hand over your own bell? Then all three of you pass.

284
00:17:06,986 --> 00:17:07,705
[SASUKE] Already?

285
00:17:07,845 --> 00:17:11,404
[KAKASHI] It's the first time I've said that. Do not ruin it.

286
00:17:11,636 --> 00:17:17,150
It's the first team Kakashi Hatake has ever passed. He does it in ten minutes.

287
00:17:17,361 --> 00:17:19,615
[SAKURA] That was actually kind of smart, Naruto.

288
00:17:19,732 --> 00:17:21,486
[NARUTO] I know. I read it somewhere.

289
00:17:21,716 --> 00:17:25,001
[KAKASHI] Same time tomorrow. Do not be late.

290
00:17:25,135 --> 00:17:26,964
[SASUKE] You're the one who's always late.

291
00:17:27,096 --> 00:17:28,626
[KAKASHI] Right. Fair point.

292
00:17:28,757 --> 00:17:34,011
Every team before them failed. This one passed because one boy had read the file.

293
00:17:36,934 --> 00:17:40,118
That night, Kakashi stands in the Hokage's office,

294
00:17:40,118 --> 00:17:42,728
and for once he doesn't open with a joke.

295
00:17:42,967 --> 00:17:46,576
[KAKASHI] They passed. First try. Ten minutes.

296
00:17:46,824 --> 00:17:51,283
[HIRUZEN] Congratulations, Kakashi. You're finally a teacher.

297
00:17:51,517 --> 00:17:53,486
[KAKASHI] That wasn't a compliment, was it?

298
00:17:53,599 --> 00:17:55,128
[HIRUZEN] Not entirely.

299
00:17:55,283 --> 00:17:58,322
[HIRUZEN] Tell me. How did Sasuke take it?

300
00:17:58,447 --> 00:18:04,846
[KAKASHI] He called him a loser. Then he said thank you. Quietly, so nobody would notice.

301
00:18:05,066 --> 00:18:06,010
[HIRUZEN] Progress.

302
00:18:06,126 --> 00:18:09,354
[KAKASHI] Lord Third. What exactly have you let him read?

303
00:18:09,566 --> 00:18:17,180
[HIRUZEN] Only what any clerk reads. Forms. Receipts. Reports. He asked politely.

304
00:18:17,386 --> 00:18:19,292
A beat passes. Then another.

305
00:18:19,292 --> 00:18:24,125
The Third Hokage studies his pipe as if it has just told a clever joke.

306
00:18:24,363 --> 00:18:25,635
Two in the morning.

307
00:18:25,635 --> 00:18:30,457
The archive is empty, except for one filing box that isn't a filing box.

308
00:18:30,712 --> 00:18:31,691
It's a clone.

309
00:18:31,691 --> 00:18:37,341
Naruto left him behind, transformed, to finish the shelf marked off limits.

310
00:18:37,542 --> 00:18:41,906
[CLONE] Do not breathe loudly. Do not breathe at all. You're a box.

311
00:18:41,836 --> 00:18:47,970
[CLONE] Rule one, touch nothing. Rule two, touch everything. Rule three, don't get caught.

312
00:18:48,115 --> 00:18:55,482
The off-limits shelf. Twelve years of dust. And one box where a clerk in a hurry filed the wrong sheet.

313
00:18:55,482 --> 00:18:59,774
A hospital roster. Medical leave, October, twelve years ago.

314
00:18:59,992 --> 00:19:06,496
[CLONE] It's alphabetical. One line's inked out. Above it, Uzuki. Below it, Yakushi.

315
00:19:06,753 --> 00:19:10,217
[CLONE] Somebody blacked out the name. Nobody thought to re-alphabetize the page.

316
00:19:10,455 --> 00:19:15,214
[CLONE] I've filed the whole clan registry. Exactly one name fits between Uzuki and Yakushi.

317
00:19:15,437 --> 00:19:19,611
He has written that name on every form he has ever signed in his life.

318
00:19:19,852 --> 00:19:22,676
[CLONE] The leave ends October tenth. That's my birthday.

319
00:19:22,935 --> 00:19:24,754
[CLONE] Authorized by the Fourth Hokage.

320
00:19:25,294 --> 00:19:26,423
The clone pops.

321
00:19:26,423 --> 00:19:32,818
Across the village, Naruto sits bolt upright in bed, holding a memory he never lived.

322
00:19:33,047 --> 00:19:37,121
[NARUTO] Breathe. It's only a clone's memory. It's just a clone's memory.

323
00:19:37,268 --> 00:19:39,252
[NARUTO] Uzumaki. There was another one.

324
00:19:39,465 --> 00:19:45,454
Deep under the seal, in the dark behind the bars, one enormous red eye opens.

325
00:19:46,008 --> 00:19:51,326
[KURAMA] A thousand of you, brat. And every one carries a piece of me.

326
00:19:51,326 --> 00:19:54,377
[KURAMA] Did you think I wasn't reading too?

327
00:19:54,952 --> 00:20:01,926
[KURAMA] Her name was Kushina. I should know. I lived in her before I lived in you.

328
00:20:02,457 --> 00:20:09,109
Before Naruto, the Nine-Tails was sealed inside a woman named Kushina Uzumaki.

329
00:20:09,109 --> 00:20:11,411
That part is not a what-if.

330
00:20:11,629 --> 00:20:16,126
In Part Two, a twelve year old asks the Third Hokage one question,

331
00:20:16,126 --> 00:20:20,828
and the old man has to decide whether to lie to a thousand witnesses.

332
00:20:21,059 --> 00:20:23,948
[NARUTO] Old man. Who was Kushina Uzumaki?

